10.ARMSTRONG NUMBER 
You are given a 3-digit number n, Find whether it is an Armstrong number or not.
An Armstrong number of three digits is a number such that the sum of the cubes of its digits is equal to the number itself. 
371 is an Armstrong number since 33 + 73 + 13 = 371. 
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            static boolean armstrongNumber(int n) {
                int sum=0;
                int temp=n;
                while(temp!=0){
                    int rem=temp%10;
                    sum+=(rem*rem*rem);
                    temp/=10;
                }
                return sum==n;
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/armstrong-numbers2727/1


